---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../components/CtaBanner.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Brift — Bridging the Site to the Office"
  description="Why Brift was built: to give owner-run construction companies a single reliable operating hub across money, materials, workforce, and site updates."
>
  <!-- Header Section -->
  <section class="relative pt-16 pb-12 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-16 bg-bg border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-4 text-center">
      <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue bg-blue-soft px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full">
        OUR ORIGIN & PRINCIPLES
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink">
        Bridging the gap between the site and the office.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-muted max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Between what's happening on the ground and what you can see from your desk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Narrative Section -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-white border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">
      <!-- Section 1: The Problem -->
      <div class="space-y-4 reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">
          Why Brift exists
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-base text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Most construction companies don't run on software. They run on WhatsApp groups, notebooks, personal diaries, and spreadsheets that are already out of date by the time they are opened.
          </p>
          <p>
            When a contractor asks for an advance, it's checked against memory. When a supplier sends a bill, it's photographed, forwarded into a group chat, and buried under dozens of site photos. At the end of the month, the owner sits down to balance the books and discovers that materials went missing, budgets were exceeded weeks ago, and contractor accounts don't match.
          </p>
          <p>
            This isn't a failure of people or hard work. It's a records problem. Construction sites are dynamic, noisy, and fast-moving. Generic accounting software is too rigid for the field, while generic chat apps lack the financial rails needed to protect profit margins.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 2: Our Solution & Engineering Approach -->
      <div class="space-y-4 border-t border-line pt-10 reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">
          How we build differently
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-base text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Brift was engineered specifically for owner-run construction firms managing multiple active sites. We designed it around three non-negotiable principles:
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 pt-2">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg p-5 space-y-2">
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink">1. Works on the site</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Site conditions are unpredictable. Brift installs on mobile phones like an app, letting supervisors record attendance, purchases, and expenses even with zero cell signal, syncing automatically when connectivity returns.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg p-5 space-y-2">
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink">2. Verification first</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Money never moves until the owner or authorized admin verifies the bill. Removing a verified item posts an immutable reversing entry, so your historical audit trail remains untampered.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg p-5 space-y-2">
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink">3. Isolated deployments</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
                Each company gets their own tailored platform, configured to their specific roles, accounts, and reporting workflows — not a one-size-fits-all generic subscription.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 3: Founder & Contact -->
      <div class="space-y-4 border-t border-line pt-10 reveal">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">
          Direct partnership
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          Brift is presented and supported directly by founder <strong>Adnan Hisham</strong>. When you work with us, you speak directly with the team engineering your system, bringing in your past site history, and training your supervisors.
        </p>

        <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Have questions before scheduling?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-0.5">Reach out directly via phone or email.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <a
              href="tel:+919037532036"
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-white border border-line px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-ink hover:bg-bg shadow-2xs"
            >
              +91 9037532036
            </a>
            <a
              href="/book-a-demo"
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-hover shadow-2xs"
            >
              Book a Demo
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <CtaBanner />
</Layout>
